        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.27,
            0.51,
            0.402,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "At a Glance"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.537,
            0.866,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Life on the Earth exists in many forms, from simple bacteria to complex animals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.574,
            0.867,
            0.609
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Scientists classify organisms based on the cell structure, number of cells, mode of nutrition and the organism’s ecological role."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.611,
            0.867,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Whittaker’s five kingdom classification system — Monera, Protista, Fungi, Plantae and Animalia — is a simple and useful system to understand diversity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.079,
            0.696,
            0.177,
            0.916
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.079,
                0.696,
                0.177,
                0.916
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_20_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.666,
            0.865,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Kingdom Plantae is further divided into five classes — Thallophyta, Bryophyta, Pteridophyta, Gymnosperm and Angiosperm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.703,
            0.867,
            0.789
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Kingdom Animalia is divided into non-chordata (invertebrates) and chordata (vertebrates) on the basis of formation of notochord. Non-chordata (Invertebrates) has been divided into phyla — Porifera, Cnidaria, Platyhelminthes, Nematoda, Annelida, Arthropoda, Mollusca, Echinodermata."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.241,
            0.792,
            0.867,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Protochordates show a transition from invertebrates to vertebrates as they possess notochord atleast once in their life. Vertebrates are further divided into groups — fish, amphibians, reptiles, birds and mammals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.241,
            0.862,
            0.868,
            0.915
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Classification is not just about naming organisms. It helps us understand the relationships among organisms, trace the history of life on the Earth and conserve the biodiversity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
